| Spaces and line endings made regular for the HTML and SGML import: runs of spaces and line endings collapse, line endings become spaces, except inside lit and pre tags
| The net effect of this table is to eliminate all spaces and line endings
| that follow another space or line ending, except within <lit> ... </lit>
| (or pre) tags.  Surviving line endings are also turned into spaces, again
| except within lit/pre tags.
| As later defined (>=1995-12-28), also downcases within actual tags,
| eliminates all after spaces within tags, and converts some HTML tags
| to ICADD equivalents
| ---
|     font), and change to entrefs so resulting file is true ASCII;
|     1998-9-23 convert numeric entrefs 160-255 to name form;
|     discard undefined lower controls
|     tags (such as "img") to survive as LF's;
|     retain alt="..." text in generated <note><tnote>...</tnote></note> tags
|     eliminate entref processing and consideration of elements
|     in upper or partially upper case (now handled in prior step);
|     eliminate rules to discard lower controls (now done in encut8)
|     2007-8-17 MPG: Treat <u> as <other> (-> fts~u...fte~u)
| 2007-9-7 MPG: Add special treatment for <a href>
| 2007-9-11 MPG: Fixes for <a> introduced by last change
| 2007-12-28 MPG: Remove <img>
|     form, including [es~...] and [ee~...] as well as [<] and [>] commands, may
|     already be present in the input, and if so should be copied through
| ---
| States: 1 = after space (or line beginning) outside lit tags
|   2 = not after space or line beginning outside lit tags
|   3 = inside <lit> ... </lit>
|   4 = outside lit, but within a noncomment tag
|   5 = inside lit, and within a noncomment tag
|   6 = outside lit, within alt= within a noncomment tag
|   7 = inside lit, within alt= within a noncomment tag
|   8 = outside lit, within href= within a noncomment tag
|   9 = inside <a>...</a>
|  10 = inside <...> within <a>...</a>
|  11 = inside alt within <a>...</a>
|   -2 = outside lit, within a noncomment after space
|   -3 = inside lit, within a noncomment after space
|   -4 = within a nested < ... > within state -2 (for complex "!doctype"s)
|   -5 = inside <a ...>, like -2 but check for href
|   -6 = within a <a...> with a link
|   -7 = within <... > after space, within <a>...</a>
| ---
